solution:
A negative exponent takes the reciprocal, and an exponent of \(1/4\) means the positive fourth root. Since the base is positive,
\[
\left(\frac14\right)^{-1/4}
=4^{1/4}
=\sqrt{\sqrt4}
=\boxed{\sqrt2}.
\]
Thus the answer is choice E.

